# Public key(s) that sign Wrought release binaries, in OpenSSH
# allowed-signers format (man ssh-keygen, "ALLOWED SIGNERS"). Used by
# scripts/release.sh to check its own output and by users to verify
# downloads (docs/content/docs/releases.md).
#
# OWNER TO FILL IN before the first signed release: generate the release key
# offline, keep the private half out of this repository (store it as the CI
# secret RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY), and add one line of the form
#
#   wrought-release namespaces="wrought-release" ssh-ed25519 AAAA...
#
# Publish the same line on the project website too, so users can compare it
# with this file. Until a line is added, real (non --dry-run) releases fail.
